Mechanism: VLAN 5 is bridged on sshswitch between the access trunk from switch4 (eth0.5) and an upstream “bonded” trunk to router17 (bond0.5). Both sshswitch and router17 are configured with Linux bonding mode 0 (round-robin). This mode sends successive frames across both physical members and, in a multi-bridge environment, causes MAC moves and STP churn. Kernel logs show br_v5 member ports repeatedly transitioning to “disabled” then back to “forwarding,” momentarily dropping the VLAN 5 SVI and freezing traffic for a few seconds.

