[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch,router17
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the VLAN 5 gateway bridge (br_v5, 10.5.0.254) on sshswitch and its upstream link aggregation toward router17 (bond0/bond0.5 on both ends).

Mechanism: VLAN 5 is bridged on sshswitch between the access trunk from switch4 (eth0.5) and an upstream “bonded” trunk to router17 (bond0.5). Both sshswitch and router17 are configured with Linux bonding mode 0 (round-robin). This mode sends successive frames across both physical members and, in a multi-bridge environment, causes MAC moves and STP churn. Kernel logs show br_v5 member ports repeatedly transitioning to “disabled” then back to “forwarding,” momentarily dropping the VLAN 5 SVI and freezing traffic for a few seconds.

Localization: On sshswitch, /proc/net/bonding/bond0 confirms “Bonding Mode: load balancing (round-robin)” with slaves eth6/eth7; bridge membership shows both eth0.5 and bond0.5 in br_v5. dmesg on sshswitch records, at multiple times, “br_v5: port … entered disabled state” for both eth0.5 and bond0.5 and bond0 being unregistered/re-registered. Switch4 shows synchronized port state changes at the same timestamps, confirming impact on the access side. Router17 likewise runs bond0 in round-robin, amplifying the instability.

Root cause: Misconfigured link aggregation (mode 0 round-robin) between sshswitch and router17 causes L2 instability and periodic br_v5 port disable/enable events.

Corrective fix: Reconfigure the inter-switch aggregation to a stable mode: either 802.3ad (mode 4 with LACP) on both sshswitch and router17 or active-backup (mode 1). Ensure STP/RSTP is enabled and consistent, or temporarily remove bond0.5 from br_v5 until proper aggregation is deployed. This will stop the gateway “blinking” for VLAN 5 clients (PC1/PC2). === END ===